Reason: place_empty and place_free walked every instance in the room and worked out each one's bounding box.
move_bounce_all asks place_empty four times, and AM2R calls it from every debris piece, ice shard and spark that
touches a wall: during a power bomb in rm_a3a19 the debris's bounces cost 3.2 ms a frame on the real Wii, and the
collision phase 7.5 ms, so most of those frames ran late. The two now look in the grid cells under the box, plus the
grid's dirty list, when those hold fewer instances than the room; the answer is only whether anything blocks, so the
order instances are tested in cannot change it. Otherwise they walk the room as before.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

